-- handled: same error call as noisy, but this module declares its own
-- Error { … } block — which mangles to the module's error bag along
-- with everything else, so the module handles its own errors. The
-- error tuple's leading atom travels with the bag: Error ++ suffix.
(Boom, reply) : [lob reply (AboutTo,); error ("bad", reply)]

Error { (Error, msg, reply) : lob reply (Caught, msg) }
